![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The manual construction of the JSON string for the tool call is fragile. Specifically, `tool_call.name` is not being escaped, which can lead to invalid JSON if the name contains special characters like double quotes. This can cause tool calling to fail. It's safer to use the `tojson` filter on string values that are part of the JSON structure to ensure they are correctly escaped.

```
            {{- '{"name": ' ~ (tool_call.name | tojson) -}}
            {%- if tool_call.arguments is defined -%}
                {{- ', "arguments": ' -}}
                {%- if tool_call.arguments is string -%}
                    {{- tool_call.arguments -}}
                {%- else -%}
                    {{- tool_call.arguments | tojson -}}
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {{- "}\n" -}}
```

